{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe","id":1410584,"title":"Any chance the WoD and CoD settings will ever be squished into one universe?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-26T17:14:02-07:00","id":1410584,"title":"Any chance the WoD and CoD settings will ever be squished into one universe?","content":"Like DC did with Earth-One and Earth-Two back in the Eighties?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T17:19:54-07:00","id":1410586,"title":"","content":"Daeva becomes Toreador<br /> Gangrel<br /> Mekhet becomes Lasombra<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Ventrue<br /> <br /> Invictus merges with the Camarilla<br /> Carthians become a faction of the Anarchs<br /> Circle of the Crone, Lancea et Sanctum, Ordo Dracul all become independent sects<br /> <br /> The two different versions of werewolves, mages, changelings, mummies and demons all coexist with each other (maybe the Atlantean mages become a separate Tradition with their own Paradigm)<br /> <br /> Just a thought. Do you guys really need two separate game lines about playing monsters in today\u2019s world?<br /> <br /> Not being snarky. Really curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 08-26-2020, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T17:30:44-07:00","id":1410588,"title":"","content":"Probably not, just because both lines have their fanbases and will probably continue producing STV material. <br /> <br /> But in the long run, there's no telling what the current or future IP owners may decide to do with some theoretical 6th edition of Vampire or what have you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T17:36:29-07:00","id":1410589,"title":"","content":"Maybe the more basic question I don\u2019t get is what is the fundamental difference between these two game lines that makes some people prefer one over the other? (I like WoD better but only cause I know it better.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T17:37:39-07:00","id":1410590,"title":"","content":"To me CoD seems like a copy of WoD with some stuff changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T20:48:45-07:00","id":1410605,"title":"","content":"The major lines came out with transition guides if you wanted to do crossover between game lines. <br /> <br /> Personally I like Cod better because it's a more (imo no edition waring here thank you) a more focused on what you are then what the over all meta plot is kinda product. Werewolf the Forsaken dosen't have you be an eco warrior in a war you already lost, Mage the Awakening is actually about magic and not reality wish granting. Vampire is about maintaining humanity without copouts like paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T21:28:39-07:00","id":1410606,"title":"","content":"The way I see, CoD is WoD before the metaplot. Not exactly the same, but what I expected from those games before I learned about the metaplot at least.<br /> <br /> Personal horror and not a peon in a chess game<br /> Dealing with your dual identity and not ecoterrorists<br /> Magic and power and not killing man in black<br /> <br /> To be honest, the way they deal with the several stereotypes of monsters (including mages as \u201cwitches and warlocks\u201d from fairy tales) in CoD is a much more open and at same time focused that it was in WoD. For example, the single origin of all the vampires is abandoned, opening space for many mythologies and conceptual vampires without needing to link them to Cain. This many little things makes the entire feeling of the setting more interesting.<br /> <br /> I never played CoD, and played WoD for years, but I do prefer CoD since I first saw the book in a Sydney RPG shop back in 2005 just for removing all carried stories (basically for removing Ravnos it would gain my hearth, but taking Tremere and Giovanni with them was a life quality jump).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T04:54:00-07:00","id":1410656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe?p=1410605#post1410605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The major lines came out with transition guides if you wanted to do crossover between game lines. <br /> <br /> Personally I like Cod better because it's a more (imo no edition waring here thank you) a more focused on what you are then what the over all meta plot is kinda product. Werewolf the Forsaken dosen't have you be an eco warrior in a war you already lost, Mage the Awakening is actually about magic and not reality wish granting. Vampire is about maintaining humanity without copouts like paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for answering. I hadn\u2019t thought of it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T04:55:35-07:00","id":1410657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe?p=1410606#post1410606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see, CoD is WoD before the metaplot. Not exactly the same, but what I expected from those games before I learned about the metaplot at least.<br /> <br /> Personal horror and not a peon in a chess game<br /> Dealing with your dual identity and not ecoterrorists<br /> Magic and power and not killing man in black<br /> <br /> To be honest, the way they deal with the several stereotypes of monsters (including mages as \u201cwitches and warlocks\u201d from fairy tales) in CoD is a much more open and at same time focused that it was in WoD. For example, the single origin of all the vampires is abandoned, opening space for many mythologies and conceptual vampires without needing to link them to Cain. This many little things makes the entire feeling of the setting more interesting.<br /> <br /> I never played CoD, and played WoD for years, but I do prefer CoD since I first saw the book in a Sydney RPG shop back in 2005 just for removing all carried stories (basically for removing Ravnos it would gain my hearth, but taking Tremere and Giovanni with them was a life quality jump).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I do prefer WoD but CoD is fun to read (I never actually played it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T08:37:10-07:00","id":1410687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe?p=1410605#post1410605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The major lines came out with transition guides if you wanted to do crossover between game lines.<br /> <br /> Personally I like Cod better because it's a more (imo no edition waring here thank you) a more focused on what you are then what the over all meta plot is kinda product. Werewolf the Forsaken dosen't have you be an eco warrior in a war you already lost, Mage the Awakening is actually about magic and not reality wish granting. Vampire is about maintaining humanity without copouts like paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to say that the cosmic shenanigans of both Mage lines could theoretically make some kinda of &quot;Infinite Crisis&quot; situation in your own setting with crossovers between the WoD and CoD, using the Translation Guides to figure out how the rules might interact.<br /> <br /> I first discovered World of Darkness through Bloodlines, but I started with CoD on tabletop actually because everything online said it was set up better for crossover, mechanically at least; I like my horror-fantasy kitchen sinks. I've since transitioned over more to Old WoD these days because I enjoy the over-the-top comic-book-style metaplot, and while Mage is one of my favourite game-lines in either version, I prefer the concepts and cosmology of Ascension more than Awakening. Definitely agree with the above that CoD is (generally, not always) more about personal horror, along with the more mundane horror of things just being vaguely and generally bad, rather than having some identifiable schemer/ancient evil/Lovecraftian horror that embodies everything bad in the universe.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, I think I mostly like CoD better, but I'd probably port over the Difficulty mechanic because I like the variability it adds to rolls; I have a bit of a complexity-addiction though, and they probably dropped that because most people prefer it that way lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T10:22:27-07:00","id":1410704,"title":"","content":"Definetly the Mage Cosmology is more interesting in Ascension, maybe because I am biased, but the supernal realms are just boring. If I was going to run a astral exploration chronicle, I would put the supernal as The deep end of the equivalent Umbras. Strige would be the deep of underworld, Arcadia would be Arcadia, etc.<br /> <br /> On the mechanics side, beside the way they are more compatible between splats, the \u201csingle variable\u201d way to handle difficulties is more interesting as I see. It was annoying to set target number and number of successes, there was no good explanation (at least to my 14 yo brain) to why it would require more successes and not a higher target number. To be fair, I learned the mechanics in two very different times of my life, as a teenager that only played D&amp;D and as a young adult that had played many more games and valued the story over violentia gratuita.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T11:30:40-07:00","id":1410719,"title":"","content":"To the general question in the title?<br /> <br /> 0%<br /> <br /> As a purely business matter, there's no evidence that there's enough people that want a merged universe to make up for all the WoD fans and CofD fans that don't want that (keeping in mind that there are plenty of people that are both and don't want a merger too).<br /> <br /> Both lines have sufficient customers bases to continue making books for both and remain profitable.<br /> <br /> Unless something in these factors changes there's zero reason to merge them, so Paradox isn't going to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe?p=1410586#post1410586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daeva becomes Toreador<br /> Gangrel<br /> Mekhet becomes Lasombra<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Ventrue<br /> <br /> Invictus merges with the Camarilla<br /> Carthians become a faction of the Anarchs<br /> Circle of the Crone, Lancea et Sanctum, Ordo Dracul all become independent sects</div> </div> </div> </div>So, while I'm trying my best to treat this fairly because I know you mean well: did you consider how much this doesn't sound like a merger of WoD and CofD, but killing Requiem and looting its corpse for WoD use? Every change here defaults towards VtM absorbing VtR things, and nothing of VtR actually coming to prominence in the &quot;merger.&quot;<br /> <br /> As someone who's favorite WW based Vampire game/edition is currently VtR 2e... what appeal does this have to me at all? How does this improve my play experience with this new merged Vampire?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The two different versions of werewolves, mages, changelings, mummies and demons all coexist with each other (maybe the Atlantean mages become a separate Tradition with their own Paradigm) </div> </div> </div>This strike me as very simplistic. Why would the Lost coexist with the Kithain? The Kithain have figured out how to have literal Arcadian Fae infiltrate the world by possessing human bodies and destroying the lives of the humans that were meant to be in them. No Lost would stomach that. And that's just one example.<br /> <br /> And again, you end with &quot;the CofD thing is second fiddle to the WoD thing.&quot; Why would Awakening fans want to play a game where the Diamond Orders are reduced to just another Tradition/Craft?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you guys really need two separate game lines about playing monsters in today\u2019s world? </div> </div> </div>1) The were never intended to coexist. When the CofD first game out, the first core book was just titled World of Darkness, because the original WoD had been concluded. The new WoD was meant to start over. For seven years it was the WoD with no competition. Then in 2011 they decided to do V20 as a one-off thing. When they exploded, and W20 exploded, the 20th line became a thing and suddenly two things that weren't meant to be in publication with each other at the same time were.<br /> <br /> 2) This actually made the CofD way stronger as a separate game because it pushed the CofD writers to create greater differences between the two and explore different game play experiences and themes. One of the exceedingly frustrating parts of how so many of these conversations go, is that it feels like it's always &quot;Everything ever created for the WoD, game books, comics, novels, video games, interviews, blog posts, etc.&quot; vs, &quot;a review of the first two CofD books written by someone that was admittedly still peeved that the WoD was concluded.&quot; 16 years of the CofD being around, and it feels like nothing beyond year 1 (which was not a great open for the CofD) gets counted.<br /> <br /> 3) Need isn't the issue. These are niche luxury products we play for fun. Want is the issue. Do I want more than one game that tackles the idea of playing monsters in today's world? Yes! Variety is good. The WoD isn't for everyone, the CofD isn't for everyone, both combined aren't for everyone. Even if the CofD and WoD weren't both being made, there's tons of other games out there that explore similar spaces. This is fertile ground within the small market that is non-D&amp;D TTRPGs, and there's no reason to act like only one game can be cultivated from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T12:52:10-07:00","id":1410749,"title":"","content":"Now, what I think will happen is all WoD will move to a *5, as V5 did and W5 is going to do. WoD will leave OPP, not entirely, but the core books will, and we will have CoD and WoD getting more and more mechanically and conceptually different.<br /> <br /> WoD more focused on the distinct meta plots, not trying to merge the splats at all, except by not negating their existence of the others. Modiphius did a interesting job with V5, with new mechanics and a new meta-plot/redict that bright new players while keeping most of the established fan base. With W5 we probably will get M5 if we have good sells.<br /> CoD will grow in depth, with more options and more interaction between the splats. OPP is doing a very interesting job on CoD with the Dark Eras, Contagion and new splats. We can see WW trusts OPP on doing both, but it\u2019s a better business plan to split the effort in different fronts, it makes the total production faster and free WW of a dependency on OPP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T16:52:43-07:00","id":1410780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe?p=1410719#post1410719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the general question in the title?<br /> <br /> 0%<br /> <br /> As a purely business matter, there's no evidence that there's enough people that want a merged universe to make up for all the WoD fans and CofD fans that don't want that (keeping in mind that there are plenty of people that are both and don't want a merger too).<br /> <br /> Both lines have sufficient customers bases to continue making books for both and remain profitable.<br /> <br /> Unless something in these factors changes there's zero reason to merge them, so Paradox isn't going to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, while I'm trying my best to treat this fairly because I know you mean well: did you consider how much this doesn't sound like a merger of WoD and CofD, but killing Requiem and looting its corpse for WoD use? Every change here defaults towards VtM absorbing VtR things, and nothing of VtR actually coming to prominence in the &quot;merger.&quot;<br /> <br /> As someone who's favorite WW based Vampire game/edition is currently VtR 2e... what appeal does this have to me at all? How does this improve my play experience with this new merged Vampire?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This strike me as very simplistic. Why would the Lost coexist with the Kithain? The Kithain have figured out how to have literal Arcadian Fae infiltrate the world by possessing human bodies and destroying the lives of the humans that were meant to be in them. No Lost would stomach that. And that's just one example.<br /> <br /> And again, you end with &quot;the CofD thing is second fiddle to the WoD thing.&quot; Why would Awakening fans want to play a game where the Diamond Orders are reduced to just another Tradition/Craft?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1) The were never intended to coexist. When the CofD first game out, the first core book was just titled World of Darkness, because the original WoD had been concluded. The new WoD was meant to start over. For seven years it was the WoD with no competition. Then in 2011 they decided to do V20 as a one-off thing. When they exploded, and W20 exploded, the 20th line became a thing and suddenly two things that weren't meant to be in publication with each other at the same time were.<br /> <br /> 2) This actually made the CofD way stronger as a separate game because it pushed the CofD writers to create greater differences between the two and explore different game play experiences and themes. One of the exceedingly frustrating parts of how so many of these conversations go, is that it feels like it's always &quot;Everything ever created for the WoD, game books, comics, novels, video games, interviews, blog posts, etc.&quot; vs, &quot;a review of the first two CofD books written by someone that was admittedly still peeved that the WoD was concluded.&quot; 16 years of the CofD being around, and it feels like nothing beyond year 1 (which was not a great open for the CofD) gets counted.<br /> <br /> 3) Need isn't the issue. These are niche luxury products we play for fun. Want is the issue. Do I want more than one game that tackles the idea of playing monsters in today's world? Yes! Variety is good. The WoD isn't for everyone, the CofD isn't for everyone, both combined aren't for everyone. Even if the CofD and WoD weren't both being made, there's tons of other games out there that explore similar spaces. This is fertile ground within the small market that is non-D&amp;D TTRPGs, and there's no reason to act like only one game can be cultivated from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Idk all this, or at least I didn\u2019t think about it. You make some very good points.<br /> <br /> And you\u2019re totally right about Changeling. I was thinking there would be two different Arcadias, but it was kind of a half baked idea (tbh I was a little buzzed when I wrote this, I had to edit like four times to fix all the typos) and it was definitely biased toward WoD and I think in general it wouldn\u2019t be a very good idea. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 08-27-2020, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T16:58:47-07:00","id":1410782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe?p=1410590#post1410590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me CoD seems like a copy of WoD with some stuff changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of that is that a fair amount of CoD's initial design and development was a direct reaction to certain parts of the just ending WoD. Much fewer clans/tribes/etc. over all. A lack of meta plot and a much looser over all setting. And mechanics that made crossover much easier. (Awakening, especially, I suspect, has a pretty objective mystic reality as a reaction to Ascension's consensual reality.) I think some of it was also an effort to try different ideas. But at the same time, they were trying to keep a lot of the elements that had helped define White Wolf's WoD lines back in the 90s. <br /> <br /> While I'm much more a fan of WoD, partially because I grew up playing it and there's just a lot of elements I enjoy, I still have a lot of the 1st ed CoD books, and have found them incredibly useful as idea fodder for my WoD games over the past 15 years. Hunter the Vigil and Changeling the Lost are probably my favorites from the imprint. Requiem books have given me a lot of ideas for Masquerade, and I crib certain parts of Forsaken's lore for Apocalypse (such as Father Wolf, and adapting the five spirit wolf patrons of the tribes into the embodiments of the Garou Auspices). The last few times I was able to run Ascension, I adapted a lot of Awakening's Sphere levels/mechanics to Ascension's nine Spheres (and ended up changeling Entropy to Fate). Geist also inspired me to cut Wraith's legions down to just six. <br /> <br /> However, I will note that I find much of the font and text style of Awakening to be utterly infuriating because it is so damn difficult for me to read, especially in less that perfect lighting. <br /> <br /> Now if you will excuse me, I have to leave the cave and take my dinosaur for a walk.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T20:47:51-07:00","id":1411043,"title":"","content":"I only recently got into the general landscape of World of Darkness 3 years ago. WoD and CofD have their different niches entirely and have different fanbases that don't have the same views. Merging is a bad idea and frankly the new edition of Vampire can be seen as a soft CofD in oWoD already with so many mechanics from there stuffed into it. Admittedly as someone who is in the oWoD camp there are a few lines in CofD I like better than their counterparts; How Changeling is handled in CofD is much, much more better. Demon the Descent was also better than DTF. I also liked how the Vampires in Requiem didn't have consolidated creation mythos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T09:39:03-07:00","id":1411082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe?p=1411043#post1411043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only recently got into the general landscape of World of Darkness 3 years ago. WoD and CofD have their different niches entirely and have different fanbases that don't have the same views. Merging is a bad idea and frankly the new edition of Vampire can be seen as a soft CofD in oWoD already with so many mechanics from there stuffed into it. Admittedly as someone who is in the oWoD camp there are a few lines in CofD I like better than their counterparts; How Changeling is handled in CofD is much, much more better. Demon the Descent was also better than DTF. I also liked how the Vampires in Requiem didn't have consolidated creation mythos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I like exactly the opposite of what you like. But thanks for answering \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T22:07:16-07:00","id":1453325,"title":"","content":"In my WoD4x/WoDD&amp;D i kinda did, sort of...<br /> A funny accident, but still good! As the &quot;NWoD&quot; books were getting rolled out, i was trying to keep up by binging the free pdfs &amp; stuff online. I got Time of Thin Blood, but some craziness in my RL at the time meant i was not able to keep up with the many 'end of the world' books. So i was forced to fill in gaps by using the wikis.<br /> None of the materials i had/saw/seen/read had the actual &quot;MEMO\u2122&quot; that they were in fact ending the WoD completely and starting over. By the time i did, i had already begun incorporating the NWoD elements into my ongoing WoD universe.<br /> As with some of the comments before me, VTR factions became Sects, and some of the VTR clans &amp; bloodlines became bloodlines in mine.<br /> Werewolf was &amp; is a bit messier, with its changes. TBH, i have not really used much from it. I basically treat the Uratha as having branched off way, way back, and generally don't play w/Garou. So Garou are the main shifters in my WoD, but there is Uratha so if i get a player that prefers them to Garou, they have the option.<br /> I retconned the Atlantean Orders as having been around, and made fifth columns in both the Traditions &amp; the Technocracy; they are the new BIG BAD Mages on the block...<br /> All the 'end times' s### kicked the gates open for The Lost to return to Earth as the Dark Fae were.<br /> I didn't get into NWoD's Wraiths, but i did add Prometheans.<br /> So, in short, My WoD survived the many bad things of 1999-2006, and the 2nd round in 2008-2012.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\ud83d\udd3a\ud83d\udd3a\ud83d\udd3a\ud83d\udd3aPrimarch Anubis\ud83d\udd3a\ud83d\udd3a\ud83d\udd3a\ud83d\udd3a<br /> \ud83d\udd34\ud83d\udd34\ud83d\udd35\ud83d\udd35\u26aa<br /> \u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26aa\u26aa<br /> \ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26035-primarch_anubis","name":"Primarch_Anubis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T05:12:21-07:00","id":1453346,"title":"","content":"Oh wow! Cool. I kinda gave up on this idea though. People convinced me that both settings are awesome in their own way and squishing them together would do a disservice to both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T07:46:20-07:00","id":1453363,"title":"","content":"I would say it is more likely they ask that the CofD does more to distinguish the IP and trade dress in a future edition.<br /> <br /> Requiem, Forsaken, and Awakening began as spiritual successors to Masquerade, Apocalypse, and Ascension, and there are still a lot of overlap/points of consumer confusion. You see people confused over the differences on forums and social media all the time. All three games diverged over time, to the point where the 2nd editions are clearly a different take on the same core idea rather than an iterative reskinning. I actually think that the divergences grew to the point that the parts of the old games are actually detrimental to the new ones. I think (just as an example), that Awakening would be a stronger game without Awakenings, as strange as that might sound. You'd have to change the name, of course.<br /> <br /> The Promethean and beyond games are hard to confuse with their predecessor. You'd have to tweak or rename some things here and there, but they can largely stand as-is.<br /> <br /> So I wouldn't be shocked if at some point the CofD got renamed to, I don't know, &quot;Night Horrors&quot; or &quot;Dark Chronicles.&quot; And the X:theY naming convention changed to Night Horrors: Vampire, or Dark Chronicles: Blood and Smoke. Change the system to appear less like the old Storyteller system and maybe carve out the 50% of Requiem/Forsaken/Awakening that are still derived from the original, emphasizing the differences, just to reduce brand confusion.<br /> <br /> I can even see in my mind's eye a Requiem 3rd that cut most of the Masquerade baggage and still preserved the core theme, or an Awakening 3rd without the stuff that carried over from Ascension, and it's still an occult detective game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T13:48:42-07:00","id":1453402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe?p=1453363#post1453363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say it is more likely they ask that the CofD does more to distinguish the IP and trade dress in a future edition.<br /> <br /> Requiem, Forsaken, and Awakening began as spiritual successors to Masquerade, Apocalypse, and Ascension, and there are still a lot of overlap/points of consumer confusion. You see people confused over the differences on forums and social media all the time. All three games diverged over time, to the point where the 2nd editions are clearly a different take on the same core idea rather than an iterative reskinning. I actually think that the divergences grew to the point that the parts of the old games are actually detrimental to the new ones. I think (just as an example), that Awakening would be a stronger game without Awakenings, as strange as that might sound. You'd have to change the name, of course.<br /> <br /> The Promethean and beyond games are hard to confuse with their predecessor. You'd have to tweak or rename some things here and there, but they can largely stand as-is.<br /> <br /> So I wouldn't be shocked if at some point the CofD got renamed to, I don't know, &amp;quot;Night Horrors&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Dark Chronicles.&amp;quot; And the X:theY naming convention changed to Night Horrors: Vampire, or Dark Chronicles: Blood and Smoke. Change the system to appear less like the old Storyteller system and maybe carve out the 50% of Requiem/Forsaken/Awakening that are still derived from the original, emphasizing the differences, just to reduce brand confusion.<br /> <br /> I can even see in my mind's eye a Requiem 3rd that cut most of the Masquerade baggage and still preserved the core theme, or an Awakening 3rd without the stuff that carried over from Ascension, and it's still an occult detective game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! That\u2019s really helpful to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T03:48:58-07:00","id":1453910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe?p=1411082#post1411082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. I like exactly the opposite of what you like. But thanks for answering \ud83d\ude0a.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why they shouldn't be merged. <br /> <br /> Now, I personally wouldn't mind updates of the Translation Guides, as well as additional Translation Guides for those lines that never got them: the Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage Translation Guides were all WoD Revised Editions vs. CofD 1st Editions, and both universes have moved on since then. But I'm not expecting that to ever happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T05:08:46-07:00","id":1453919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe?p=1453910#post1453910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's why they shouldn't be merged. <br /> <br /> Now, I personally wouldn't mind updates of the Translation Guides, as well as additional Translation Guides for those lines that never got them: the Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage Translation Guides were all WoD Revised Editions vs. CofD 1st Editions, and both universes have moved on since then. But I'm not expecting that to ever happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I no longer think merging them is a good idea.<br /> <br /> Why isn\u2019t that gonna happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T10:23:02-07:00","id":1453948,"title":"","content":"Because Onyx Path has been pushing for the two to be distinct, to the point that they make significant changes in the second editions of the Chronicles lines to differentiate them more. The Translation Guides, by their mere existence, tend to create the impression that they're <i>not</i> that different. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> On the flip side though, White Wolf seems to have a penchant for poaching ideas from Chronicles for use in their \u201cfifth edition(s)\u201d, such as the inclusion of Blood Potency in V5; and I've heard rumors of some possible developments for W5 that sounds suspiciously like stuff I've seen in Forsaken. I can't provide any specifics, because I honestly wasn't paying that much attention to it; but I <i>do</i> recall getting that impression. <br /> <br /> So it <i>is</i> possible that you might end up seeing, not so much a <i>merger</i> of the two settings, as a sort of <i>chase</i>, with Onyx Path struggling to make the CofD stand apart from the WoD and White Wolf seeking to make the World of Darkness look more like the Chronicles. <i>Maybe</i>. <br /> <br /> I could see that because the Chronicles <i>did</i> start out as a reimagining of the WoD, by the same teams that had been working on the original setting, with the goal of actually doing what they wished they <i>could have done</i> with the original games if not for the need to remain more or less consistent with pre-existing material. So it makes sense to me that the WoD 5e folks might want to incorporate some of the innovations that the CofD came up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T12:00:17-07:00","id":1453957,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s interesting. Thanks. So it\u2019s kinda like White Wolf does want them to merge into one universe. I think they\u2019re thinking what I thought when I started this thread: do we really need two RPG lines about supernatural monster protagonists existing in today\u2019s world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 07-01-2021, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T12:21:09-07:00","id":1453958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe?p=1453957#post1453957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s interesting. Thanks. So it\u2019s kinda like White Wolf does want them to merge into one universe. I think they\u2019re thinking what I thought when I started this thread: do we really need two RPG lines about supernatural monster protagonists existing in today\u2019s world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, there are, what, at least a dozen such RPGs? The WoD/CofD family are just the most well known, but there's a whole bunch of takes on the secret monster/urban fantasy/monster PoV horror genre.<br /> <br /> They're in a tough position. If you wanted to consolidate the two lines, you'd have to create a blended version, which is immediately a <i>third line</i> with its own distinctive identity and now your fanbase is split four ways with people who like the new stuff, people who liked the old new stuff, people who liked the old stuff, and people who like all three but are imprisoned by the sorcerer.<br /> <br /> In a sense they're already in that situation with Vampire. V5 was the &quot;agnostic&quot; reboot, which some people love and others hated, VtR was the &quot;clean slate&quot; reboot, which some people loved and others hated, and V20 was the &quot;faithful reproduction&quot; reboot, which carried all the flaws of the old game that people used to hate and/or love. <br /> <br /> It's a little bit of a fragmented fanbase. Had I a time machine and for some reason my mission to save humanity was re-organize White Wolf's publishing decisions circa 2003, I'd probably advise them to do things differently and/or buy Amazon stock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T02:52:09-07:00","id":1454059,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"543\" data-vbnamecard=\"543\">Professor Phobos</a> what does agnostic mean? I mean, I know what it means in religion, but what does it mean in this context?<br /> <br /> And I meant what I said earlier. I\u2019ve reconsidered my views and I don\u2019t think squishing the two game lines together would be a good idea anymore. I just think maybe White Wolf (the people who make V5) thinks it might be a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T11:02:11-07:00","id":1454093,"title":"","content":"They don't; if they did, they would have done it. White Wolf owns the right to both, and is allowing Onyx Path to continue developing the Chronicles of Darkness as they see fit. But <i>because</i> they own both, they have no qualms about taking an innovation from the Chronicles of Darkness and injecting it into the World of Darkness if they think that will benefit the latter.<br /> <br /> But make no mistake: of they <i>wanted</i> to smush the two together, there would be nothing to stop them from doing so. <br /> <br /> (For the record, White Wolf also owns the rights to Exalted, and to the Storyteller system. Onyx Path owns Scion and Trinity, and the Storypath system; in fact, they developed the Storypath system specifically because White Wolf acquired the rights to the Storyteller system, and Onyx Path needed a game engine of its own that it wasn't licensing from someone else.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-02-2021, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T11:05:25-07:00","id":1454094,"title":"","content":"That makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T20:54:49-07:00","id":1454787,"title":"","content":"If anything it feels like V5 wants to go off in its own (third) direction (and even if not, that's how some of the fandom are taking it) so I'd say there's never going to be one single 'holistic' continuity. I mean they didn't seriously try to maintain rigid continuity across multiple editions or game systems in the past either (and for good reasons.) <br /> <br /> If someone really, really wanted that I'm sure you could do it (it would be an interesting narrative challenge trying to see if you can fit all the pieces together) but how broadly accepted any such merging would be taken is another matter (As much up to the skill of the storyteller as the preconceptions of the audience, really.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T11:35:51-07:00","id":1461245,"title":"","content":"My guess is not officially, but also my guess is that the 5th ed line will do this to some extent. From what i have seen V5 has a system that is a combination of parts of both (I think the best parts). And V5 also did a lot to streamline the splats like NWoD did at the time those lines came out and it did a softish reboot of the metaplot which will probably allow them to introduce good ideas from NWoD into WoD as the line progresses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T15:30:56-07:00","id":1461275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1410584-any-chance-the-wod-and-cod-settings-will-ever-be-squished-into-one-universe?p=1454093#post1454093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(For the record, White Wolf also owns the rights to Exalted, and to the Storyteller system. Onyx Path owns Scion and Trinity, and the Storypath system; in fact, they developed the Storypath system specifically because White Wolf acquired the rights to the Storyteller system, and Onyx Path needed a game engine of its own that it wasn't licensing from someone else.)</div> </div> </div> </div>White Wolf doesn't own the rights for the Storyteller System <i>per se</i>, as Onyx Path doesn't own the rights for the Storypath system. I think the change had more to do with the continuation of the rights over the original game lines.<br /> <br /> By law game systems can't be protected by copyright, because mathematical systems can't be protected by copyright, only a given expression of those systems can. You can \u00a9 a character sheet layout and your text describing the rules, but you can't \u00a9 the idea of a Strength Attribute, or the idea of throwing Att + Abi d10s and taking how many are above a Difficulty Number as successes.<br /> <br /> The precise line is complicated, but what stopped Onyx Path wasn't copyright over the system <i>per se</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T11:59:27-07:00","id":1461738,"title":"","content":"I hope NOT!!! CWOD Is much more monomythic Then COD/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}